      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): cleanup leaked toolStartData entries on unsubscribe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe module-level `toolStartData` map retained entries when an embedded-agent subscription ended before the matching tool-end event. Long-running gateways could accumulate stale records, and `countActiveToolExecutions` could report tools from ended runs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUnsubscribe now removes `toolStartData` entries for that run using the same run-scoped key invariant as the active-count path. Entries owned by other runs are preserved.\n\nAI-assisted.\n\n## User Impact\n\nInterrupted or unsubscribed embedded-agent runs no longer leave stale tool-start tracking behind. Abort decisions keep an accurate per-run active-tool count.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression suite: `src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.unsubscribe-tool-start.test.ts` proves unsubscribe clears only the target run and preserves another run.\n- Exact reviewed head: `a9e48c4580e7dde6f7fa8fd637ea2a437a00d6d8`, based on current `main` `957cc81175a3f993118951e352fd2b13e3982487`.\n- Exact-head autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Hosted gates: [CI run 29468370781](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29468370781), green.\n",
        "branch": "fix/bug-043-toolstart-data-leak",
